course: dictionary
lesson: 10056
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the context: the other words in the sentence and the sentences around it. «Testers play the same parts again and again, trying odd things to find bugs.» Here a tester is a person, because testers play, try things and write reports.
explain: Now read «Try the tester before you buy the perfume.» The words before you buy tell you a tester is a small sample, not a person. Same word, different meaning: the clues decide which one it is.
explain: The third meaning is a tool. «Use a battery tester to check the old batteries» means a device that checks whether a battery still has power. Ask: which meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A tester is a person whose job is to test things, like games, apps, food or cars, to find problems.
fact: A tester can also be a small sample of a product, such as perfume or paint, that you can try before you buy.
fact: A tester can be a tool or device for testing, such as a battery tester.
fact: «Big games are made by teams: programmers, artists, designers, writers, sound and music people, testers, producers and more.»
fact: Before a toy reaches a shop, testers pull, drop, chew-test and even burn samples on purpose.
exercise: «Testers play the same parts again and again, trying odd things to find bugs.» What is a tester here? | A small sample of perfume | A game with a bug in it | A battery tester device | *A person whose job is to test things
exercise: «Try the tester on your wrist before you buy the perfume.» What is a tester here? | A shop worker who sells perfume | *A small sample you can try before you buy | A person who makes perfume | A tool for checking batteries
exercise: Which meaning fits «Use a battery tester to check the old batteries»? | A small sample of paint | A bug in a program | A person who tests games | *A tool or device for testing
test: «The game tester found three bugs before the game was released.» What is a tester here? | A tool for checking power | *A person whose job is to test things | A sample of perfume | A paint shop worker
test: Which meaning fits «She picked up a tester of lip balm from the shelf»? | A worker in a factory | A device for checking batteries | A person who tests games | *A small sample you can try before you buy
exam: Which meaning of tester fits «Testers pull, drop and burn sample toys on purpose to check they are safe»? | A toy shop worker who sells toys | A small sample of a product you can try before you buy | *A person whose job is to test things | A device for checking batteries
